{# Challenge shown to an anonymous visitor asking for a url that runs a search.

   Deliberately self-contained: it extends nothing and loads nothing but Google's widget.  It is
   served to clients we don't trust yet, so it shouldn't pull in the full page chrome, and on a
   wordpress-integrated install there is no chrome to pull in anyway.

   Posting the form returns to the same url, where RecaptchaService checks the token. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
    <title>Confirm you are human</title>
    <script src="https://www.google.com/recaptcha/api.js" async defer></script>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 40px 16px;
            background: #fff;
            color: #333;
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
        }
        main { max-width: 32rem; }
        h1 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin: 0 0 .75rem; }
        p { line-height: 1.5; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
        .term { font-weight: 600; }
        button { font: inherit; padding: .5rem 1rem; margin-top: 1rem; cursor: pointer; }
        .note { color: #666; font-size: .9rem; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
    <h1>Confirm you are human</h1>

    <p>
        Searching for <span class="term">{{ search_string }}</span> needs a quick check first.
        Automated traffic has been running very large numbers of searches, so a search that
        arrives straight from a url is confirmed this way.
    </p>

    <form method="post" action="{{ form_action }}">
        <input type="hidden" name="odr_recaptcha" value="1">
        <div class="g-recaptcha" data-sitekey="{{ site_key }}"></div>
        <button type="submit">Continue</button>
    </form>

    {% if failed is defined and failed %}
        <p class="note">That didn't verify. Please try again.</p>
    {% endif %}

    <p class="note">
        Already have an account? <a href="{{ path('fos_user_security_login') }}">Log in</a> and
        searches run without this step.
    </p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
